<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $26.7 mln Nov 13.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $26.7 mln Nov 13.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $26.7 million surplus on November 13, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the central bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON NOVEMBER 14</p>
<p>Exports: $151.6 million</p>
<p>Imports: $243.6 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $665.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $546.7 million</p>
<p>Surplus: $26.7 million</p>
<p>NOVEMBER DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $1.551 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $1.520 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $3.713 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.326 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.418 billion</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415</p>
</text>
